From cf2c4df24587f87555ba713a5ccbcf73c8561c5a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 1aeo <github@1aeo.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 08:43:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/13] relay_metrics: Count tunneled directory requests and
 responses

tor_relay_streams_total{type="BEGIN_DIR"} counts BEGIN_DIR streams, but
nothing after that: whether a stream ever sent a usable request, whether
it asked for an ordinary directory document or an onion service
descriptor, and whether the response left the directory connection.

Add tor_relay_dir_requests_total{type="non_hs|unparsed"} for tunneled
requests that aren't onion service descriptor fetches or uploads (those
are in tor_relay_hsdir_get_total and tor_relay_hsdir_post_total), with
"unparsed" covering a parse_http_url() failure and a connection closed
while waiting for its request. Add
tor_relay_dir_responses_total{type="hs_descriptor|other"} for responses
fully handed to their stream in connection_dir_finished_flushing(), which
does not mean the client received them.

Only tunneled (BEGIN_DIR) connections are counted, so on a public relay a
BEGIN_DIR stream lands in exactly one of these request types or the onion
service families, or is still waiting for its request. The counters live
in the relay module, with stubs for the dircommon callers.

Part of #41339.
